the sixth episode of the mandalorian  second season  chapter 14 the tragedy was an  action-packed installment sure to please  boba fett fans  and as always there were plenty of  easter eggs tucked away in the margins  here are a few you may have missed tease  at the beginning of the mandalorian  second season  chapter 14 finally brought boba fett  back to the forefront of the star wars  universe in grand fashion  he not only reclaimed his armor but also  took the fight to a platoon of hapless  stormtroopers  reminding everyone why he's considered  the most ruthless bounty hunter  in the galaxy still while this wasn't a  specially big return for boba fett  one couldn't help but notice how the  memory of his father jango fett  dominated much of his screen time this  is evident first when mando questions  him on his mandalorian heritage  boba fett replies i'm a simple man  making his way to the galaxy  like my father before me fans of attack  of the clones know that this is  reminiscent of a conversation that  django had with obi-wan  where he said i'm just a simple man  trying to make my way in the universe  additionally boba mentions that much  like his ship slave 1  his famed arm is set as a hand-me-down  once belonging to his father  fett also explains to mando that  contrary to popular belief  jango didn't steal it rather he earned  it years ago during his days as a  foundling  boba says his father jango even served  during the mandalorian civil wars  an event alluded to now and again in the  clone wars animated series  the conflict was a reason for the divide  between sateen cruise of mandalore  and governor preet vizsla of concordia  after mando recovers his best scar spear  boba fett says he wants mando to take a  look at something  then presses a spot on his armor just  above his wrist a sequence of texts  written in the mandalorian language  flashes into the air  boba explains that's his chain code  which has been encoded into the armor  for 25 years  the audio description on disney plus  calls it a lineage tree  as boba points out the code mentions  both him and his father  but what about the other lines star wars  fans online made quick work of  translating the chain code into english  it's incomplete but some of it makes  sense from left to right it reads  foundling took into the year the concord  dawn  mentor just father fett boba fett  but what does all that mean first  mentioned in the clone wars and first  appearing in rebels  concord dawn as an outer rim territories  planet led by fen rao mandalorian  protectors ruled concord  dawn in the age of the empire on concord  dawn the empire crossed paths with rao  and fellow mandalorian warrior sabine  wren who gave the darksaber to bokehtan  before it somehow ended up in maf  gideon's hands additionally  concord dorm was the home planet of  reiko hardin a bounty hunter known as  the marksman of concord dawn who once  tried to assassinate obi-wan in an  episode of the clone wars  concord dawn is also allegedly where  jango fett himself was born  according to the canon reference book  star wars the complete visual dictionary  new edition  the mentor jazz part of the lineage tree  is likely a reference to justin mariel a  mandalorian warrior also born on concord  dawn  and an important figure to the phet  family in legends canon  mario first appeared in the comic django  fett's open seasons in 2002  initially serving as a journeyman  protector a low-level cop essentially  but real wound up killing a corrupt  high-ranking officer driven by his  unshakeable morals  for this he was exiled from concord dawn  and eventually joined the mandalorians  mariel later rose in the ranks to become  the sole leader of the mandalorian  people  he established a mandalorian honor code  resulting in tension from the new  mandalorian group and the death watch  splinter terrorist group  led by the vicious tor vizsla when war  erupted mourinho headed back to concord  dawn where he saved and orphaned django  fed from a death watch attack  mario became django's adoptive father  and mentor but was killed six years  later  by vizsla django later avenged mariel's  death  then rose to become the new leader of  the mandalorian people  there were a few minor easter eggs  hidden in chapter 14 worth mentioning  boba fett says that the appearance of  moth gideon's light cruiser isn't a  spice dream  a reference to spice the most popular  illicit substance in the star wars  universe  first mentioned way back in a new hope  the drug is a staple in star wars  stories  and the pivotal part of solo was even  set in a spice mine  blue butterfly-like insects similar to  the one flying near grogu  appeared on endor in the battlefront  video game series and a slightly  different blue species appeared in the  clone wars  the e-web heavy repeating blaster used  by the stormtroopers in this episode  before it was crushed by a raiders of  the lost ark style runaway boulder  first appeared in the empire strikes  back at the battle of huff  and finally the design of those dark  troopers sure called to mind tony  stark's iron man armor especially while  in flight  this makes sense of course considering  iron man director and happy hogan  portrayer john favreau  is the showrunner for the mandalorian  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the mandalorian are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

